  "id": "screwit",
  "neon": "#7dff6a",
  "note": "SCREW IT — the chemical supply on Ironside Street. A trade counter with a works behind it.\n\n⚠ THE PLANT IS THE BUILDING. Everything a chem supply is actually for happens above the parapet:\nthe scrubber that takes what comes off the drums, and the stack that puts the rest over the roofs.\nThe arm drew a depot with drums outside, which is the storage and not the trade.\n\n⚠ THE STACK IS TALLER THAN THE SCRUBBER AND THAT IS NOT A STYLE CHOICE. A fume stack has to clear\neverything near it or it is a nuisance rather than a stack, and on this street the thing it has to\nclear is the Embassy's shoulder two doors down. It is the second vertical on Ironside — the first is\nthe crane at Salvage Rites — and the two are deliberately different shapes so the street does not\nread as having one landmark twice.\n\n⚠ AND THE HAZARD PLATE IS THE SMALLEST SIGN AND THE ONE PEOPLE READ. A works does not sign itself\n(see UNSIGNED_TRADE) — it carries a placard, a unit number and nothing else. This one signs itself\nanyway because it sells over a counter, which is the stated exception, so it gets both.",
